      'The evidence comes from Phillippa Lally’s 2009 study at University College London, which Scientific American walked through in detail. Volunteers chose a new daily behaviour — drinking a glass of water, doing fifty sit-ups, eating a piece of fruit at lunch — and reported each day whether it felt automatic. The study ran long enough to watch habits actually form, rather than guessing.',
      '## The 18-to-254-day reality',
